# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
build/
dist/

# The GDC cohort is fetched on demand, never vendored -- it is not ours to
# redistribute. See odrl_fl/tcga.py.
data/

# Results are ignored by default, but the small ones that back a claim in the
# README are kept: the CSVs an experiment produced and the figures rendered
# from them, ~90 KB in total. A repository whose argument is that claims should
# be checkable has to ship the numbers behind its own. Anything larger or
# regenerable stays out.
results/*
!results/*.csv
!results/figures/
results/figures/*
!results/figures/*.svg
# The cluster campaign is the exception to the exception. Each array task
# writes its own shard, and the joined lattice at 20 federations x 5
# replicates is roughly 20 MB -- regenerable from `slurm/10_groundtruth.sbatch`
# and far past what belongs in a repository. The five-federation
# `groundtruth.csv` it supersedes stays, because the paper's figures are
# rendered from committed numbers.
results/shards/
results/groundtruth_wide.csv

# Slurm writes one pair of logs per array task.
slurm/logs/
# Exported policy-carrying model bundles.
artifacts/
*.log

# Tooling
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/
.mypy_cache/

# PDFs in paper/ are not committed. The published versions of our own papers
# belong to their publishers to distribute, the personal documents are not
# repository material, and a compiled sac2027.pdf is build output.
paper/
